  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Robbie Ray turned a tight ballgame into a shutout, and the Giants seized the smallest opening.",
    "what_this_means": "Ray delivered eight scoreless innings on two hits. A masterclass in control when precision mattered most. Jung Hoo Lee drove in the go-ahead run in the second and added another hit later. The Giants led from that moment forward, never trailing, never tied after the first inning. They left runners in scoring position in both the fourth and sixth. Ten total RISP plate appearances that produced just two runs. It was not efficient. It was enough. Caleb Kilian closed it out cleanly in the ninth. This is a team that does not need to bury anyone. A one-run lead, a shutdown starter, and a clean finish. That's the margin they're working with right now, and it held.",
